!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/link/valid/a-payload-of-the-kernels-constructor-constructs-the-documents-own-refined-one-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/link-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §3.3, [TSON-SCHEMA] §3.4.1 (the wait order, proposed), [TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.7"
  description: """
    A construction's payload is read in the namespace of the schema that writes it, its own entries included. `rows`
    refines `meta.array`, so it IS-A `meta.type`, and a construction of it is a value at each `meta.type` position the
    kernel's `meta.record` payload has: a field's type in place, and an element type in place inside another
    construction. `post` is written first: reading its payload selects `rows` by its tag and waits on it being ready.
    """
  valid: {
    binds: [post rows]
  }
}
